<title>JAPAN: Tokyo oil products market closed for holiday.</title>
<headline>Tokyo oil products market closed for holiday.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-05-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Tokyo oil products market is closed for a national holiday on Monday.</p>
<p>Trade will resume on Tuesday.</p>
<p>On Friday, naphtha prices were mostly stable in quiet trade.</p>
<p>Open-spec naphtha for second-half July was nominally assessed at $209.00/$210.00 per tonne, barely changed from late Thursday's levels.</p>
<p>In inter-month spreads, first-half August was valued 25 to 50 cents above first-half July.</p>
</text>
